  "body": "## Independent research scope and authority\nStacked **draft** on [PR #152](https://github.com/cosmosapjw-quantum/rei_bianchi/pull/152) at exact parent `bbbd18b5c16eff70bc32ba4296360dceb9060ec4`. No changes to v3/rux DAG, PR #150 FLRW production, PR #151 microphysics, or any active NCP job. This is **not** a production EoR or a temperature-history claim.\n\n## Theory and actual implemented physics\n- Retain the exact LRS Bianchi I null-ray energy/direction characteristic and original Verner-1996 H I, He I, He II donor in PR #152.\n- Add *coupled*, time-varying absorber stocks HI\u2192HII, HeI\u2192HeII\u2192HeIII with photon consumption and electron census, instead of the prior prescribed frozen neutral stock.\n- Each reaction `photon_r + target_i -> ion_i + e` has `dN/dX=dM/dX=-k_i(X) N M`; derive an exact positive pair map, including equal-population limit. Verified symbolically with Wolfram Language derivative residual 0 and positivity domain.\n- Split every ray-specific ionization threshold event; integrate the exact pair flows by symmetric forward/reverse half-step Strang composition with midpoint Verner rate coefficients. Source-free photon geometrical work uses exact characteristic energy differences before/after midpoint chemistry.\n- Preserve HI+HII, HeI+HeII+HeIII, photon+free-electron count, and split photon energy = surviving photons + binding energy + photoelectron excess heating + anisotropic redshift work. The *discrete* energy invariant is algebraically closed and by itself is **not** proof of continuum accuracy.\n- **Diagnosed and repaired a real false-anisotropy defect**: unsymmetrized per-ray reaction composition caused FLRW spurious `Pi/U~1e-8`. Grouping exactly equal absorption characteristics (all angles at FLRW, \u00b1mu mirrors in LRS) before each nonlinear pair map preserves isotropy and reflection symmetry.\n\n## Executed verification and evidence\n**21/21 new pytest PASS in ChatGPT execution container**, Py3.13.5 / NumPy2.3.5 / SciPy1.17.0 / pytest9.0.2, not user Ubuntu/NCP. Independent source-equivalent direct continuous RHS solved by SciPy Radau, with exact threshold event partition, rtol=2e-11 / atol=2e-13. Refined \\Delta X_max=0.005 maximum absolute mixed-state/energy difference:\n- signed s/H -0.04: `3.91965e-6`;\n- 0: `4.13072e-6`;\n- +0.04: `3.94854e-6`.\n\nNormalized final electron stock `0.075176194 / 0.075175622 / 0.075176115`, corresponding `Pi/U=+0.043021788 / ~0 / -0.041437005`. Number/electron residual ~1e-16 and split-energy ledger residual ~1e-14 eV/n\u2605. Tests include stiff rate, exact logistic reaction, nucleon conservation, 2nd-order trend vs Radau, \u00b1mu reflection, FLRW isotropy and invalid domains. All artifacts saved as code, tests, raw 15-row JSON and Python stdout, manifest and Korean derivation under `research/lrs_threshold_oracle_20261015/`.\n\n**Source identities:** GitHub fetched file blob SHAs exactly match tested sandbox Git blobs for all eight newly committed files. A 16,633-byte ZIP of the complete v3 outputs was uploaded to the connected Google Drive folder `REI_RESEARCH_BACKUPS/rei_bianchi/REI_LRS_DYNAMIC_20261016` and its bytes were read back to confirm SHA256 `21508b7e7fb1712fd56077735dd9595b46d9ef239c58ff48de8facc3f3d36402`. A separate persistent Library copy also exists.\n\n## Runtime limitation\nThe user's Ubuntu Desktop Commander reached its **monthly tool-call quota** immediately after an initial untested `dynamic_chemistry.py` was written to the local PR152 worktree. **Do not claim the new code was run on that Ubuntu checkout or NCP**. No reconnect/retry was attempted. The sandbox-tested and GitHub-published version is authoritative for this PR. After quota reset, reconcile the local untracked file before switching branches or pulling; do not overwrite without examining the diff. NCP SSH access and Rust 1.99 availability were confirmed by read-only probes prior to quota exhaustion; no new NCP numerical run was launched in this invocation.\n\n## Scientific exclusions and next action\nNo recombination, sources, thermal feedback, scattering, self-consistent expansion, native Rust coupling, or physical EoR history. Need genuine source-native PR150 H/He chemistry + photon transport adapter, first matched fixed-state then dynamic neutral stock comparison; separately validate cosmological thermal and ion histories before production claim.\n\n**Reproduce** from PR152-base working tree, with the branch's added sources:\n```bash\ncd research/lrs_threshold_oracle_20261015\npython3 -m pytest -q tests/test_dynamic_chemistry.py\npython3 run_dynamic_benchmark.py\n```\n",
